    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56de1324_a351a516",
        "filename": "radio/1.1/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 117,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-29T18:12:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we have the indication one then?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 68,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "285644a6d7f111b626e4dd7d95e7fdbfaa505e5e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29d0a569_0bf2b76a",
        "filename": "radio/1.1/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 117,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-31T18:00:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, there are two uses for the indication.\n\n1) For *reasons* we can\u0027t rely on waiting for the session to be ACTIVE before the response is sent (it could take too long depending on the architecture... I\u0027ve heard worst-case of a few seconds), so the Indication can tell us that it has become active or simply give us a handle to identify the request and say \"pending\". In the wifi case there is also an UNSOL just in case the request is slow.\n\n2) If the data call ends, then the keepalive session should also end, and AP should be notified. There is also a STOP, but that\u0027s inherently racy, so we\u0027ll call it if the session is still active, and we\u0027ll just have to swallow some errors on STOP (which is OK/WAI).",
      "parentUuid": "56de1324_a351a516",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 68,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "285644a6d7f111b626e4dd7d95e7fdbfaa505e5e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db7c7d5f_592cef35",
        "filename": "radio/1.1/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 117,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-01T05:09:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we always use the indication then, as in have sessionHandle only there? And keep the response only as an ack without any parameter? Having the same parameter in both seems a little odd.",
      "parentUuid": "29d0a569_0bf2b76a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 68,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "285644a6d7f111b626e4dd7d95e7fdbfaa505e5e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
